# SEO — Portfolio Site

## What SEO means here

Search engines and social platforms need **crawlable, accurate metadata** and **semantic HTML** so the portfolio ranks for name + role queries and renders rich previews when shared.

This is a **Vite SPA** (single page, hash anchors). Crawlers see `index.html` first; content in React must still use proper headings and accessible text — not images alone.

Reference: `DESIGN.md` §11.

---

## Recommendations

### Document metadata (`index.html`)

- **Title**: `{Name} — {Primary role}` (unique, ≤60 chars)
- **Meta description**: hero pitch, **120–155 chars**, active voice, no keyword stuffing
- **`lang`**: set on `<html>` (e.g. `en`)
- **Canonical**: `<link rel="canonical" href="https://{production-domain}/" />`
- **Open Graph**: `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image` (1200×630), `og:url`, `og:type=website`
- **Twitter**: `twitter:card=summary_large_image`, mirror title/description/image
- **Favicon**: SVG + fallback; `theme-color` optional

Derive title/description from `siteContent` (`name`, `title`, `pitch`) — keep `index.html` in sync after content changes or generate at build time.

### Static assets (`public/`)

- `robots.txt` — allow `/`, point to sitemap
- `sitemap.xml` — at minimum the homepage URL with `lastmod`
- OG image at a stable path (e.g. `/og-card.png`)

### Structured data

Add JSON-LD `Person` in `index.html` (or injected at build):

```html
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "…",
  "jobTitle": "…",
  "url": "https://…",
  "sameAs": ["https://github.com/…", "https://linkedin.com/in/…"]
}
</script>
```

Use real profile URLs from `siteContent`; omit fields you cannot verify.

### On-page semantics (components)

- **One `<h1>`** per page — hero name/headline only
- Section titles: `<h2>`; subsections: `<h3>` — never skip levels
- Wrap page in `<main id="main">` (already in `App.tsx`)
- Section `id`s match nav hash targets (`#projects`, `#experience`, …)
- Images: descriptive `alt` (project title + context); decorative images use `alt=""`
- Links: meaningful text ("View on GitHub"), not "click here"
- Project cards: title + description are indexable text, not only visuals

### Content (`src/content/`)

- **Pitch** doubles as meta description — front-load role + value prop
- Project **descriptions**: concrete outcomes, stack, and scope in 1–2 sentences
- Avoid duplicate titles across projects/sections

### Performance (SEO-adjacent)

- Lazy-load below-fold media; prefer WebP/AVIF for photos
- `width`/`height` on images to reduce CLS
- Preconnect only to origins actually used (fonts, analytics)

