## Patterns ✅

```html
<!-- index.html -->
<title>Your Name — Senior Software Engineer</title>
<meta name="description" content="Senior Software Engineer building scalable products with LLMs, RAG, and AI-augmented engineering." />
<meta property="og:image" content="https://example.com/og-card.png" />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://example.com/" />
```

```tsx
// Hero — sole h1
<h1>{siteContent.name}</h1>
<p>{siteContent.title}</p>

// Section — h2 with stable id for nav/anchors
<section id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
  <h2 id="projects-heading">Projects</h2>
</section>

// Project image
<img src={project.imageUrl} alt={`${project.title} — ${project.description}`} loading="lazy" />
```

---

## Anti-patterns ❌

| Don't | Why |
|-------|-----|
| Multiple `<h1>` or skipped heading levels | Breaks outline; hurts accessibility and SEO signals |
| Generic title (`Portfolio`, `Home`) | No ranking signal for name/role searches |
| Meta description >160 chars or duplicated across pages | Truncated in SERPs; looks spammy |
| `og:image` relative URL or missing dimensions | Broken/unstable social previews |
| Keyword stuffing in title, description, or alt text | Penalized; reads poorly |
| Empty or filename-only `alt` (`screenshot.png`) | Lost context for crawlers and screen readers |
| Critical text in images/Canvas only | Invisible to crawlers |
| `noindex` on production homepage | Blocks indexing entirely |
| Hash-only URLs as canonical for distinct content | v1 is fine for one page; don't use `#/page` as separate SEO URLs without SSR/prerender |
| Blocking `robots.txt` on `/` or missing sitemap | Reduces discoverability |
| Stale `index.html` meta after DB/content rebuild | Mismatch between SERP snippet and live site |

---

## When adding routes (post-v1)

- Give each public route its own title, description, canonical, and OG tags
- Prefer path URLs (`/projects/foo`) over hash routes for indexable pages
- Consider prerender/SSR or a post-build meta injection step for SPAs
